    "turn_text": "President Joe Biden is still against ending the filibuster, according to White House Press Secretary Jen Psaki. Psaki said Monday per the Hill, his preference is not to make changes to the filibuster rules. And he believes that with the current structure that he can work with Democrats and Republicans to get work and business done. Ending the filibuster would mean that Democrats could pass legislation with a mere 50 votes if Vice President Kamala Harris was the tiebreaker.",
